.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "ssize_t libusb_get_device_list (\fBlibusb_context\fP * ctx, \fBlibusb_device\fP *** list)"

.PP
Returns a list of USB devices currently attached to the system\&. This is your entry point into finding a USB device to operate\&.

.PP
You are expected to unreference all the devices when you are done with them, and then free the list with \fBlibusb_free_device_list()\fP\&. Note that \fBlibusb_free_device_list()\fP can unref all the devices for you\&. Be careful not to unreference a device you are about to open until after you have opened it\&.

.PP
This return value of this function indicates the number of devices in the resultant list\&. The list is actually one element larger, as it is NULL-terminated\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIctx\fP the context to operate on, or NULL for the default context 
.br
\fIlist\fP output location for a list of devices\&. Must be later freed with \fBlibusb_free_device_list()\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
the number of devices in the outputted list, or any \fBlibusb_error\fP according to errors encountered by the backend\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void libusb_free_device_list (\fBlibusb_device\fP ** list, int unref_devices)"

.PP
Frees a list of devices previously discovered using \fBlibusb_get_device_list()\fP\&. If the unref_devices parameter is set, the reference count of each device in the list is decremented by 1\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIlist\fP the list to free 
.br
\fIunref_devices\fP whether to unref the devices in the list 
.RE
.PP

.SS "unsigned long libusb_get_session_data (\fBlibusb_device\fP * dev)"

.PP
Returns the backend-specific identifier of the underlying system device tree node\&. Can be used to find the corresponding system device and directly query it (or access it otherwise) when and if necessary\&.

.PP
Relevant backends:
.IP "\(bu" 2
Darwin: IOKit \fRsessionID\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Windows WinUSB: \fRDEVINST\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Linux, BSD: \fRbusnum << 8 | devnum\fP
.PP

.PP
Since version 1\&.0\&.30, \fBLIBUSB_API_VERSION\fP >= 0x0100010C

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdev\fP a device (must not be null) 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
the backend-specific device identifier 
.RE
.PP

