.SS "int libusb_endpoint_set_raw_io (\fBlibusb_device_handle\fP * dev_handle, uint8_t endpoint, int enable)"

.PP
Enable/disable RAW_IO for an endpoint on an open device\&. Only endpoints using the WinUSB driver support RAW_IO, for all other backends/drivers this function will return an error code\&.

.PP
Using RAW_IO can greatly improve USB throughput by directly passing transfer requests to the underlying USB driver instead of queuing them in WinUSB\&. This can be particularly useful for high-throughput devices like cameras or oscilloscopes\&.

.PP
Transfers submitted to the endpoint while RAW_IO is enabled will fail unless they adhere to the following rules :
.IP "\(bu" 2
The buffer length must be a multiple of the maximum endpoint packet size 
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBlibusb_get_max_packet_size\fP\&.
.RE
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
The buffer length must be less than or equal to the value returned by \fBlibusb_get_max_raw_io_transfer_size\fP\&.
.PP

.PP
This option should not be changed when any transfer is in progress on the specified endpoint\&.

.PP
Fails if the interface the endpoint belongs to isn't claimed, 
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBlibusb_claim_interface()\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
